//
// PROBE: the stack words the corpus never reaches.
//
// `rust_multistack` is the **third** registration tier — ERRATA records that a
// scan of only `rust_multistackvm` and `Bund` reports these as unregistered —
// and most of it is untouched by the corpus. These are the ones Bund2
// implements, exercised here so the implementation is checked against the
// oracle rather than against my reading of it.
//
// Two behaviours worth pinning because they are easy to get backwards:
//
//   - **`swap` takes a count**, it is not the classic two-element exchange
//     (reference/rust_multistack/src/stdlib/swap.rs:23-29); `swap_one` is that.
//     `10 20 30 1 swap` answers `10 20 1 30`, and the stack comes back the
//     size it went in — which is why its declared effect is 2->2 and not 1->0.
//   - **`clear` empties the current stack**, so the box after it is empty and
//     everything pushed before is gone.
//
"probe: swap takes a count, swap_one exchanges" println
10 20 30 1 swap debug.display_stack
clear
10 20 swap_one debug.display_stack
clear
"probe: dup_one, dup_many, drop" println
7 dup_one debug.display_stack
clear
7 3 dup_many debug.display_stack
clear
1 2 3 drop debug.display_stack
clear
"probe: rotate" println
1 2 3 rotate_current_left debug.display_stack
clear
1 2 3 rotate_current_right debug.display_stack
clear
"probe: the workbench round trip" println
42 . take println
"probe: return moves to the workbench, take brings it back" println
5 return take println
